Device modules now describe their capabilities: the new :attr:`DeviceModule.protocols <peat.device.DeviceModule.protocols>` attribute (a list of :class:`~peat.module_protocol.ModuleProtocol`) declares the protocols, transports, and default ports a module uses to pull and push, and scanning protocols are derived from ``ip_methods`` and ``serial_methods``. Capabilities can be queried with ``DeviceModule.get_operations()``, ``get_protocols()``, ``get_ports()``, ``get_method_names()``, ``get_protocol_details()``, and ``get_capabilities()``, and ``SerialMethod`` has a new ``protocol`` field. ``scan``, ``pull``, and ``push`` have a new ``-p/--protocols`` argument (and ``protocol_filter`` option) to only use modules that use the given protocols, ports, or port ranges for that command and type of targets, e.g. ``peat pull -p ftp 161/udp``; if the option can't be loaded, PEAT exits with an error instead of using all modules. The new ``--module-info <module>`` argument shows a module's operations, protocols and ports, identification methods, supported models, and parsable files, and ``--list-modules`` and ``--list-all`` now show the operations and protocols of each module.
